Q: java code for Given an unsorted integer array nums. Return the smallest positive integer that is not present in nums.
Logic : "I checked every number from 1 to n.If I find a missing one, return it.If I finish checking and didn't find anything missing, then 1..n are all present, so return n+1.
To sort first : ARRAY LENGTH = n

1. Only numbers 1..n matter. Ignore -ve, 0

2. Number x has a home:
      x → index x- for ex : number is 2 then its home is 2-1 =1

3. Put every useful number in its home.

4. Scan:
      index i should contain i+1

5. First wrong position:
      answer = i+1

6. If nothing is wrong:
      answer = n+1

------------------------------------------------
class Solution {
    public int firstMissingPositive(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length;
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++)
        {
            while(nums[i]>=1 && nums[i] <=n && nums[nums[i]-1]!=nums[i])
            {
                int index = nums[i]-1;
                int temp = nums [i];
                nums[i] = nums[index];
                nums[index] = temp;

            }
        }
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++)
        {
            if(nums[i]!=i+1)
            {
                return i+1;
            }
        }
        return n+1;
        
    }
}
